node_modules/
build/
dist/
coverage/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env*
!.env.example

# admin/ is tracked in git (CEO decision 2026-09-30) so it has a backup — it is still never
# deployed publicly: the GitHub Pages build only builds the root app. admin/.env stays ignored
# via the .env* rule above.

# CEO-private notes — kept out of git so they can never reach GitHub by accident.
/Drake/ceo's eyes only/

# Never pushed to GitHub (CEO, 2026-10-02: "add drake, the context.mds and the claude.md to a gitignore,
# never push those"). The repository is public. The local working branch still tracks the files already
# committed, to keep their history: add new ones there with `git add -f`. Publish the app with
# `node scripts/publish-app.mjs`, never by pushing the working branch. A pre-push hook refuses any push
# that would carry these paths.
/Drake/
/CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md

# Local tooling state (Claude Code worktrees, Vite dep cache, wrangler's local cache) — not project source.
/.claude/
.vite/
.wrangler/
# Wrangler's local secrets file, if anyone makes one.
.dev.vars*
